(*"external_reference_schema.message"
A message is a communication that is addressed to a system in order to trigger some action. The result of such an action is an external item or identification.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.message.__note"
The role of *message* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.source_item"
A **source_item** type allows for the designation of an <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> or a <<express:external_reference_schema.message,message>>.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source"
An **external_source** is the identification of a source of product data that is not the EXPRESS schema to which the exchange conforms.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.__note"
The product data may conform to some other part of this International Standard.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.source_id"
the identification of the **external_source**.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **external_source**.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.description.__note"
This attribute is an upwardly compatible addition to *external_source* as specified in ISO 10303-41:1994.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.wr:WR1"
Each **external_source** shall be the <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute.described_item,described_item>> in at most one <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>>.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.wr:WR1.__note"
The <<express:basic_attribute_schema.description_attribute,description_attribute>> data type is defined in <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> of this document.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source.wr:WR1.__note"
A template for constraining the population of the entity data types defined in the <<express:basic_attribute_schema,basic_attribute_schema>> is described in annex E.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship"
An **external_source_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> with a description of their relationship.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.__example"
One <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> may be a subset of another <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>>. This entity may be specialized to specify such a relationship.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.__note"
The role of *external_source_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **external_source_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **external_source_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.relating_source"
one of the instances of <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.relating_source.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.related_source"
the other instance of <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.related_source.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item"
An **externally_defined_item** is the identification of information that is not explicitly represented in a given exchange and that is not defined in the annotated EXPRESS schema to which the exchange conforms.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item.item_id"
the string that specifies the identification of the referent item.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item.source"
an <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> that contains the referent item.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship"
An **externally_defined_item_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> with an identification and description of their relationship.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.__note"
The role of *externally_defined_item_relationship* can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or by default, in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.__note"
Relationships represented using this entity may be parent child relationship. Annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity specify whether or not the relationship is directed.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.__note"
This entity, together with the <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> entity, is based on the relationship template that is described in annex E.3.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **externally_defined_item_relationship** is known.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **externally_defined_item_relationship**. The value of the attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.relating_item"
one of the instance of <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.relating_item.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references"
An **externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references** is a type of <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> that allows to define additional references providing information on the context and location of the target item within the source.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references.references"
a list of <<express:external_reference_schema.source_item,source_item>>s defining a path to the target <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item.item_id,item_id>>.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references.ur:UR1"
The list of references shall be unique.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references.wr:WR1"
An **externally_defined_item_with_multiple_references** is a type of <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item.item_id,item_id>> that adds a list of references to provide an unambiguous path in the external data. The <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item.item_id,item_id>> inherited from the <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> is the target for the reference list, but is excluded from the list itself. The list ends at a entity data type that explicitly references the target or that is explicitly referenced by the target.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.related_item"
the other instance of <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent up on the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.related_item.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.pre_defined_item"
A **pre_defined_item** is the identification of information that is not explicitly represented in a given exchange but that is defined in the annotated EXPRESS schema to which the exchange conforms.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.pre_defined_item.__example"
A reference to the colour 'red' without any definition of the associated red-green-blue values would be a *pre_defined_item* if the red-green-blue values of the colour 'red' were specified in the relevant annotated EXPRESS schema.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.pre_defined_item.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **pre_defined_item** is known.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship"
The **acyclic_external_source_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship,external_source_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship,external_source_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship,external_source_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source,external_source>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship.relating_source,relating_source>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_external_source_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:external_reference_schema.external_source_relationship,external_source_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship"
The **acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship,externally_defined_item_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship,externally_defined_item_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship,externally_defined_item_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item,externally_defined_item>> for which the function is searching in the <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship.relating_item,relating_item>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"external_reference_schema.acyclic_externally_defined_item_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified entity name of a type of <<express:external_reference_schema.externally_defined_item_relationship,externally_defined_item_relationship>> entity.
*)


